59,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option B solves the morning shoving. No one owns a spot, so no one blocks the exit.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A generates income, but the ledger is empty. We would need to levy households to start.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"Option C is fair, but the daily riders said they prefer paying. A lottery might frustrate them.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A risks social isolation. The neighbours had people stop attending meetings. I prefer B.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option B requires maintenance, but it avoids the three hours of cash reconciliation. I prefer B.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, the income from A is nice, but the administrative cost is high. B is simpler.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, B requires capital for the racks. We have no funds. We would need a one-time levy.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"@Mio, if we choose B, we need a clear plan for who maintains the racks.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@George, the lottery in C is rigid. If someone moves, the spot stays empty. B is more flexible.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, I can handle the greasing. It is only twice a year. The paperwork for B is minimal.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"The rain exposure is a problem for B, but we can prioritize the dry spots for the racks.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,The one-time levy for B is manageable. The ongoing cost of A is not.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,The history of fixed spots is broken. B resets the system. I support B.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,B keeps the community intact. No one is a debtor. I support B.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,B is the most sustainable for me. I support B.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I support B. It addresses the safety and fairness issues.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I support B. The financial risk is lower than A.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,I support B. It breaks the old pattern.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I support B. It avoids social conflict.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,I support B. It is manageable.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
